ie because we don\'t know if Charlie is blue or furry.\n9. The statement "If Charlie is nice and Charlie is big then Charlie is quiet" is not directly applicable to Charlie because we don\'t know if Charlie is quiet.\n10. Since we don\'t have any information that directly links Charlie\'s color to his being nice and big, we cannot determine if Charlie is blue or not.\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "Charlie is blue" is unknown.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
