first.\n\nTo determine if Bob is white, we need to check if there is any information that directly or indirectly confirms Bob\'s whiteness. Let\'s review the relevant points:.\n\n- Point 15 states that if someone is white, they are quiet. However, this does not provide any direct information about Bob being white.\n- Point 14 states that if someone is nice, they are quiet. We know Gary is nice (point 5), so Gary is quiet (point 14). But this does not help us determine Bob\'s whiteness.\n- Point 13 states that if someone is round and not smart, they are not quiet. Since Bob is smart, this point does not apply to Bob.\n- Point 12 states that if someone is quiet, they are round. Since Gary is quiet (point 14), and Gary is round (point 6), this point does not provide any new information about Bob\'s whiteness.\n- Point 10 states that if someone is green and young, they are white. We know Fiona is young (point 4), but we do not know if Fiona is green. Therefore, we cannot conclude that Fiona is white, and this does not help us determine Bob\'s whiteness.\n\nSince there is no direct or indirect information that confirms Bob is white, and we have no information that contradicts the statement, the statement "Bob is white" remains unknown.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
