ice then it is not blue.**.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Bob is not green" using the given information:.\n\n- From point 1, we know Bob is rough.\n- From point 16, if something is nice and not rough, it is red. Since Bob is rough, this condition does not apply to him.\n- From point 18, if something is rough, it is nice. Therefore, Bob is nice.\n- From point 17, if something is nice, it is smart. Therefore, Bob is smart.\n- From point 20, all blue, smart things are furry. Since Harry is blue, smart, and furry, and Bob is smart, it implies that Bob is furry.\n- From point 19, if something is blue, it is furry. Since Harry is blue and furry, and Bob is furry, it implies that Bob is blue.\n- From point 21, if something is green, it is blue. Since Bob is blue, it implies that Bob is not green.\n\nThus, based on the given information, we can conclude that Bob is not green.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Bob is not green" is true.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
