mation, we know:.\n- The lion does not chase the bear.\n- The lion does not chase the squirrel.\n- The lion is not red.\n- The squirrel is green.\n- The squirrel sees the dog.\n\nUsing the conditional statements:.\n- Since the squirrel is green, it sees the dog (from statement 20).\n- Since the squirrel sees the dog, it visits the bear (from statement 21).\n- Since the squirrel visits the bear, it sees the bear (from statement 17).\n- Since the bear sees the dog (from statement 18), the bear sees the dog.\n\nHowever, the key point is that the lion does not chase the bear, and there is no information suggesting the lion visits the bear. The only information we have about the lion\'s actions is that it does not chase the bear, and there is no other information indicating the lion visits the bear.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "The lion does not visit the bear" is true.\n\n<｜Assistant｜> <answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 29%|##9       | 175/600 [34:25<17:16,  2.44s/it]
