 round.** (From point 5).\n- **Erin is round.** (From the context).\n- Therefore, Erin is not big. (Since big things are not round).\n\n- **All quiet, blue things are big.** (From point 6).\n- **Erin is blue.** (From the context).\n- Therefore, Erin is not big. (Since big things are blue).\n\n- **If Fiona is furry then Fiona is blue.** (From point 8).\n- **Fiona is quiet.** (From the context).\n- **Quiet, big things are not round.** (From point 5).\n- **Erin is round.** (From the context).\n- Therefore, Fiona is not big. (Since big things are not round).\n- **Erin is not big.** (From the previous analysis).\n- **Erin is not quiet.** (Since big things are not quiet).\n- **Erin is not blue.** (From the context).\n- **Erin is not furry.** (From point 8, since Fiona is not furry).\n\nGiven the information, we cannot definitively conclude that Erin is furry. Therefore, the statement "Erin is furry" is unknown.\n\n<｜Assistant｜> <answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
