an use the rule: "If someone is big, they are nice." This means Gary is not nice.\n\nNext, we need to determine if Gary is kind. We know:.\n- All nice people are round.\n- Gary is round (from the context).\n\nSince Gary is round, he must be nice. However, we have already established that Gary is not nice. This creates a contradiction.\n\nGiven the contradiction, we cannot determine if Gary is kind or not. Therefore, we cannot determine if Gary is smart based on the given information.\n\nThus, the statement "Gary is smart" is unknown.\n\n<｜Assistant｜> <answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
