messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is furry. Anne is nice. Anne is rough. Anne is white. Erin is furry. Erin is rough. Erin is white. Fiona is big. Fiona is nice. Fiona is round. Harry is nice. Harry is rough. All furry things are white. If Harry is red then Harry is round. All round, red things are furry. If Harry is rough then Harry is round. Nice, red things are big. Round, red things are white. All nice, white things are red. If something is round then it is furry.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Harry is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "Harry is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, we need to carefully analyze the information provided and apply logical reasoning step by step.\n1. First, let\'s list the given facts:\n   - Anne is furry, nice, rough, and white.\n   - Erin is furry, rough, and white.\n   - Fiona is big, nice, and round.\n   - Harry is nice, rough, and (we need to determine if he is round or not).\n   - All furry things are white.\n   - If Harry is red then Harry is round.\n   - All round, red things are furry.\n   - If Harry is rough then Harry is round.\n   - Nice, red things are big.\n   - Round, red things are white.\n   - All nice, white things are red.\n   - If something is round then it is furry.\n2. Let\'s analyze the information about Harry:\n   - Harry is nice and rough, so he must be round (from the statement "If Harry is rough then Harry is round").\n   - Since Harry is round, he must be furry (from the statement "If something is round then it is furry").\n   - Now, we need to determine if Harry is red. If Harry is red, then he must be round (from the statement "If Harry is red then Harry is round").\n   - If Harry is red, he must be furry (from the statement "If Harry is red then Harry is round").\n   - If Harry is red, he must be white (from the statement "Round, red things are white").\n   - If Harry is red and white, he must be nice (from the statement "All nice, white things are red").\n   - If Harry is nice, red, and white, he must be big (from the statement "Nice, red things are big").\n3. Therefore, based on the given information, Harry is big.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe statement "Harry is big" is true.\n</answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
