wer than dogs.\n\n2. **Birds are faster than cats.**\n   - This implies that birds are faster than cats.\n\n3. **Dogs are faster than birds.**\n   - This implies that dogs are faster than birds.\n\n4. **If an animal is fast, it can catch a mouse.**\n   - This is a conditional statement that links speed to the ability to catch a mouse.\n\n5. **If an animal is not fast, it cannot catch a mouse.**\n   - This is another conditional statement that links non-speed to the inability to catch a mouse.\n\n6. **If an animal is a cat, it is not a bird.**\n   - This is a categorical statement that defines the relationship between cats and birds.\n\n7. **If an animal is a dog, it is not a cat.**\n   - This is a categorical statement that defines the relationship between dogs and cats.\n\n8. **If an animal is a bird, it is not a dog.**\n   - This is a categorical statement that defines the relationship between birds and dogs.\n\nFrom the context, we know:\n- Cats are not fast (since they are not as fast as dogs).\n- Since cats are not fast, they cannot catch a mouse (based on the conditional statement).\n\nTherefore, the statement \"The cat can catch a mouse\" is false.\n\nThe correct answer is:.\n<answer>B) False.\n</answer>",
