ings are round," we need to determine if Gary is red. However, we don\'t have any information directly stating that Gary is red. We only know that Gary is nice.\n\nFrom the rule "All cold, big things are red," we know that if Gary were big, he would be red. But we don\'t know if Gary is big or not.\n\nSince we don\'t have enough information to definitively say whether Gary is red or not, we cannot conclude that Gary is round.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Gary is round" is unknown based on the given information.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
