\n    - This is a general statement.\n\n14. **If something is furry then it is big.**.\n    - This is a general statement.\n\n15. **If something is nice then it is kind.**.\n    - This is a general statement.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the information step-by-step to determine if Dave is green:.\n\n- **Dave is furry.**.\n  - From point 3, we know Dave is furry.\n  - From point 14, if something is furry, it is big.\n  - Therefore, Dave is big.\n\n- **Dave is big.**.\n  - From point 11, if something is young, it is green.\n  - From point 12, if something is big, it is nice.\n  - From point 15, if something is nice, it is kind.\n  - Since Dave is big, we need to check if Dave is young.\n\n- **Dave is not young.**.\n  - From point 12, if something is big, it is nice.\n  - From point 15, if something is nice, it is kind.\n  - Since Dave is nice, he must be kind.\n  - Kind things are young (point 8).\n  - Therefore, Dave cannot be young.\n\nSince Dave is big and not young, we cannot conclude that Dave is green based on the given information. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
