 help you understand them better:\n\n### Examples of Syllogisms\n\n**Example 1:**\nAll mammals are animals.\nAll dogs are mammals.\nTherefore, all dogs are animals.\n\n**Explanation:**\n- **Premise 1:** All mammals are animals.\n- **Premise 2:** All dogs are mammals.\n- **Conclusion:** Therefore, all dogs are animals.\n\n**Example 2:**\nAll birds can fly.\nAll penguins are birds.\nTherefore, all penguins can fly.\n\n**Explanation:**\n- **Premise 1:** All birds can fly.\n- **Premise 2:** All penguins are birds.\n- **Conclusion:** Therefore, all penguins can fly.\n\n**Example 3:**\nAll students who study regularly pass the exam.\nJohn studies regularly.\nTherefore, John will pass the exam.\n\n**Explanation:**\n- **Premise 1:** All students who study regularly pass the exam.\n- **Premise 2:** John studies regularly.\n- **Conclusion:** Therefore, John will pass the exam.\n\n**Example 4:**\nAll students who study regularly pass the exam.\nMary does not study regularly.\nTherefore, Mary will not pass the exam.\n\n**Explanation:**\n- **Premise 1:** All students who study regularly pass the exam.\n- **Premise 2:** Mary does not study regularly.\n- **Conclusion:** Therefore, Mary will not pass the exam.\n\n**Example 5:**\nAll politicians are honest.\nAll honest people are trustworthy.\nTherefore, all politicians are trustworthy.\n\n**Explanation:**\n- **Premise 1:** All politicians are honest.\n- **Premise 2:** All honest people are trustworthy.\n- **Conclusion:** Therefore, all politicians are trustworthy.\n\n**Example 6:**\nAll students who study regularly pass the exam.\nAll students who study regularly are prepared.\nTherefore, all students who are prepared to pass the exam study regularly.\n\n**Explanation:**\n- **Premise 1:** All students who study regularly pass the exam.\n- **Premise 2:** All students who study regularly are prepared.\n- **Conclusion:** Therefore, all students who are prepared to pass the exam study regularly.\n\n**Example 7:**\nAll cats are animals.